# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: Lumen.
Package: Lumen
Section: Graphics
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Suggests: LumenRaw, LumenHEIF, LumenLens
Components: Apps.Graphics.!Lumen (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen
Description: Photo library and non-destructive photo editor
 A library of your photos (projects, albums, smart albums, stacks),
 with stars, flags, labels, captions and keywords; a viewer with loupe,
 split view and full screen; adjustments in 16-bit linear light without
 changing the file (white balance, exposure, curves, colour, noise
 reduction, sharpening, lens correction, crop, retouching and more),
 layers painted with a brush or set by a gradient or an oval, presets
 and styles; export to JPEG or PNG, and printing. Reads JPEG, PNG and
 TIFF; camera raw with LumenRaw, HEIF and AVIF with LumenHEIF, and lens
 profiles with LumenLens. Needs RISC OS 5.30 or later; built for the
 Pi 4.
Build-Map: !Lumen -> Apps/Graphics/!Lumen
Build-Notice: Lumen, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen/releases
 .
 Lumen is free software; it includes SQLite, libjpeg, libpng, zlib,
 UnixLib and GCC's runtime, each under its own licence. The licences
 follow.
Build-Copyright: !Lumen/Licences
